    "body": "<h2 id=\"h_01JEBSPNMW8W448R522FJJDJHB\">You will learn</h2>\n<p>Learn how to turn on hosted pages in your Klaviyo account. You can use hosted pages to display custom-coded consent pages to your subscribers, rather than using <a href=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005251848\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Klaviyo's default consent pages</a>.</p>\n<p>This article explains how to turn on the hosted pages setting in your account.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>If you're instead looking for more information on what hosted pages do, see <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360057676272\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">understanding custom hosted pages</a>.</li>\n<li>For guidance on creating custom hosted pages once you've enabled them, see <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005077067\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">How to build custom hosted pages.</a>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JEC0C3YTCJ8Q7487PRHRD71J\">Turn on hosted pages</h2>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-requirements ignore-for-search\">\n<p>Hosted pages are available for paid accounts who have passed account verification. If you do not fit this criteria, you will not see the ability to enable this setting.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Before you can replace one of your account's default consent pages, you must enable hosted pages. To enable hosted pages:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Click your organization name in the bottom left corner.</li>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Settings &gt; Other &gt; Consent pages</strong>.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/34267032329499\">\n</li>\n<li>Select <strong>Enable Custom Pages</strong> to turn this feature on and add the Hosted Pages tab to your account.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Next, head to <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005077067#h_01J5970D8JJCQ078TWYT1ADHV9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">how to custom code consent pages</a> to begin creating your custom page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JEBSPNMW556JB28KFNPGPSYG\">Disable hosted pages</h2>\n<p>If you want to turn off or remove a hosted page, do not delete the page HTML. Instead, follow these steps:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Settings &gt; Other</strong>.</li>\n<li>In the <strong>Consent pages</strong> tab, find the <em>Subscribe page </em>section. </li>\n<li>Open the dropdown next to the <strong>Edit page</strong> button. </li>\n<li>Select <strong>Remove Hosted Page</strong>. <br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28705637334171\" alt=\"Edit page dropdown highlighting the option to remove a hosted page\">\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JEBSPNMWT5M7ATK4MTP2D4C7\">Additional resources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005077067\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">How to custom code consent pages</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005251848\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Understand opt-in pages for a list</a></li>\n</ul>",
    "user_segment_ids": []
  },
